From: StellarSeal <emnoigi1452@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 13:10:06 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 095/139] fix(lighting): keep deferred light replay in queue
 order after a chunk reloads

A chunk that unloaded while queued kept its old slot in the ready queue. When it reloaded and was queued again, the stale slot made it replay before chunks queued in between, breaking the oldest-queued-first order. Each slot now carries a never-reused sequence number and is skipped once the chunk is cleared.

Replay order is documented as grouped per chunk (entries keep recording order within a chunk, chunks replay in readiness order), not global recording order. Tests pin that contract and compare 300 random operation sequences against a plain reference model.

